{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-q-connection","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical $q$-deformed connection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb"],"tags":["connection","deformation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalQConnection","text":"categorical-q-connection.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-connection.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:categorical-q-connection\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code> be a categorical connection on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> the Reeb derivation. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed connection</strong> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\nabla_q =  q^{-1}\\nabla + (1 - q^{-1})(\\iota_\\xi \\nabla)\\varTheta_A.</code></pre>\n<p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_q = \\nabla</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-connection.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"3.18.3"}
